+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-11-add-hourly-rental/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/index.ts` parses periods with `parseMidnight` (UTC midnight only) and prices whole days in `price`. Bookings
+store normalized ISO strings and overlap is a half-open comparison on milliseconds, so it already works for
+any instants.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Period kinds**: replace `parseMidnight` by a parser accepting UTC times on the hour (minutes, seconds and
+  milliseconds zero; same offset rules as today: `Z` or `+00:00`/`-00:00`). A period is whole-day when both
+  ends are at midnight, hourly when its length is under 24 hours and both ends are on the hour, and invalid
+  otherwise. A midnight-to-midnight period of under a day (e.g. 00:00 to 06:00 the same day) is hourly, since
+  it is shorter than a day; whole-day periods are therefore always multiples of 24 hours.
+- **Pricing**: hourly total is `hourlyPrice * hours`, checked with `Number.isSafeInteger`; no discount.
+  An item without `hourlyPrice` throws on an hourly period.
+- **Registration**: `hourlyPrice` optional; when not `undefined` it must be a non-negative safe integer.
+  The stored item keeps it only when given.
+- **Availability**: uses the same period parser; for an hourly period, items without an hourly price are
+  excluded (assumption: they cannot be rented, so they are not available). Whole-day behavior is unchanged.
+- **Mixed bookings**: no change; hourly and daily bookings of one item block each other through the existing
+  overlap check.
+- TypeScript strict, Node standard library only, no runtime dependency.
+
+## Risks
+
+- Previously rejected periods are now valid when on the hour and under a day (e.g. 10:00 to the next midnight);
+  an existing availability test expecting a throw for a 10:00 start was changed to 10:30.
