@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and the desk has to turn them away because rentals can only
+be priced by whole days. Customers must be able to rent by the hour.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice` (integer euro cents, not negative): the cost of one hour.
+- A rental shorter than a day (less than 24 hours) whose `start` and `end` fall exactly on the hour (UTC) is
+  priced at the item's hourly price for each hour. No long-rental discount applies.
+- An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour: `quote` and `book` throw for it.
+- `availability` accepts the same hourly periods; items without an hourly price are not offered for them.
+- Whole-day rentals are unchanged.
+
+In scope: the optional `hourlyPrice`, hourly periods in `quote`, `book` and `availability`, validation, tests.
+Out of scope: season (April to October) enforcement, cancellation, customers and lessons, persistence,
+hourly discounts, rentals of a day or longer that are not whole days, and changes to the daily price rules.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `equipment-rental`: equipment registration, rental periods, quote, booking and availability gain hourly
+  rentals.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `Equipment` type, period parsing, pricing, `addEquipment`, `availability`.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests.
+- Existing behavior for equipment without `hourlyPrice` and for whole-day periods is unchanged.
